local cleanupText={en={ ["CLEANUP_HELP"]="HOW TO USE\n/surveys opens Survey Sidekick. Surveys & Maps is the combined inventory tab. Click a zone to expand its surveys and treasure maps. Zones remember their expanded state; unknown locations are grouped last. Unidentified surveys and unopened treasure maps have a separate group. Use Hint for directions and open those containers manually from your backpack.\nFilter by item type, Backpack + Bank / Backpack / Bank and Survey Type. Use Reset Filters to show everything again. Your tab and filters save per character.\nSelect a row. Hint shows item details. Open Survey / Open Map displays the carried item's original picture. Map Pin previews its location. The coin previews recall cost; the wayshrine icon travels to the nearest unlocked wayshrine at normal ESO cost. Locations require LibTreasure. Actions appear only when available.\nOpen your personal bank to update its snapshot. Bank-only items can be hinted or pinned when their location is known; withdraw them before opening or traveling with them. Closed-bank counts are last-seen, not live.\n\nCOLORS & SIZE\nChoose a color preset or mix background, title and border colors. Background Opacity and Button Opacity are separate sliders. Labels and survey names stay readable. Size and Reset buttons are in the same menu. Settings save for this character.\n/surveys opacity 100 restores the background. /surveys buttons 100 restores buttons, including when they were made invisible.\n/surveys scale 80 restores default size. Minimize shows your selected item plus the run's timer and material total. Gathering keeps tracking while minimized.\n\nSET A COLLECTION GOAL\nOpen Current Run. Choose Survey Type, material and quantity, then Set Goal. Start / Resume counts gathered materials; Pause stops tracking; Finish Run saves your report. The Hoard Report includes your saved runs, exports and Compare Runs.\n\n/surveys inventory - combined inventory tab\n/surveys colors - Colors & Size\n/surveys help - these instructions\n" },de={},fr={},es={}}
